================================================================================
Downloaded at run time (not part of this package)
================================================================================

Embedding model Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2
  Source:  https://huggingface.co/Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2
  License: Apache-2.0
  Fetched by @xenova/transformers the first time semantic search is used and
  kept in that library's cache. Not fetched when semantic search is disabled.

On-demand Tree-sitter grammars
  Hesman downloads a grammar the first time a project contains files of that
  language, unless downloads are turned off (HESMAN_GRAMMARS_OFFLINE=1). Every
  grammar is the `.wasm` asset of the grammar's own upstream release, pinned by
  URL and sha256 in grammars.json, which also records its repository, revision
  and license. Hesman writes a NOTICE.txt with that information next to the
  downloaded files in the grammar cache. The pinned grammars are under the MIT
  License, except:

  https://github.com/elixir-lang/tree-sitter-elixir (Apache-2.0)
  https://github.com/tree-sitter-grammars/tree-sitter-hcl (Apache-2.0)

libvips (through the `sharp` dependency of @xenova/transformers)
  `sharp` (Apache-2.0) downloads a prebuilt copy of the libvips image library
  when it is installed. libvips is under LGPL-3.0-or-later and is loaded as a
  separate shared library; its own third-party notices are installed with it
  (node_modules/sharp/vendor/<version>/<platform>/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md).
  Hesman does not call it: it is present only because the embedding library
  depends on `sharp`.

